 #:seon.task{:name "a-datahike-query-walks-every-retained-result-bucket"
             :plan "A one-clause query with a new argument value costs 0.38 MB and 0.2 ms on default, 75 times the 5 KB direct datoms lookup it needs (defn-why, 2026-10-08, 400 queries under JFR): 57% is datahike.query/result-cache-get -> inheritable-entry -> compatible-source-keys?, which walks every retained result-cache bucket (lru/weighted-entries) and allocates subvec/mapv members per bucket before checking this query's cache key (reference-code/datahike/src/datahike/query.cljc:3030-3086, pin 86c3301a00); 25% is get-or-create-plan building a new plan because substituted constants are part of the plan key (query.cljc:3608-3634). Every Seon read through `seon.db/q` pays both, so cost follows retained cache size and argument values, never the query. Fix in the Datahike fork: index inheritable buckets by cache key (or check (get entries cache-key) before the member comparison), and key plans by the query with constants as bound inputs. Done when a fresh-argument one-clause query allocates under 50 KB with the query-cache inheritance regressions green. Read `seon.db/vector-query-call` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/defn-why/defn-why.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "every-index-node-access-updates-an-lru-map"
