 #:seon.task{:name "transaction-stamp-attributes-outlive-their-producer"
             :plan "`:seon.db.transaction/ms`, `:calls`, `:hot` and `:repeated` have had no producer since `seon.db/stamp-transaction` began writing cost entities (`:seon.fn.cost/entity`, card FEEDBACK-LOOP stage 5), but cannot leave their schema yet. (1) Publication runs on the live JVM: while default runs the older `seon.profile/transaction-observation` it still stamps them, and a candidate without their declarations refuses task indexing ('The attribute has no registered schema', bin/seon check operator-check-20261010T094705.882). (2) Retiring a tuple-typed attribute refuses adoption: `seon.cluster/attribute-retraction` ends with `[:db/retractEntity attribute]`, whose `:db/tupleTypes` datom Datahike retracts through the search pattern `[e :db/tupleTypes [:db.type/symbol :db.type/string :db.type/long :db.type/long]]`, which `datahike.db.search/validate-pattern` refuses ('Bad format for value in pattern, must be a scalar, nil or a vector of two elements': a vector value passes only for a tuple attribute; operator-check-20261010T094530.336, `seon.cluster/retire-attributes!`). Done when default runs a commit without the producer, `validate-pattern` (our fork) accepts the vector values of `:db/tupleTypes` and `:db/tupleAttrs`, and the four attributes leave `resources/seon/schemas/seon.db.transaction.edn`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-first-read-of-a-branch-head-derives-its-schema"
